{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_10f056634a8ba8b8c19d9a383d353e5e14f763387c0d820f7213d2807bd6f8fb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The --cost endpoint returns per-backend token counts, request counts, cost, an anthropic_equivalent figure, and total savings as JSON."},{"claim_ids":["clm_55127b79e3a893c302f1682bde7603b03b196c7e3f8c500e5d3d9d7e654ed110"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Prerequisites are a logged-in Claude Code install, a claude.ai subscription (the remote bridge is Anthropic infrastructure), Node.js 18+ for the proxy, and backend API keys such as DEEPSEEK_API_KEY."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6f7da39702c1469dbdc0ad7fcd32088c414bb9e2c039a57a1c5f896117ebd39f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Setup involves obtaining a DeepSeek API key, setting DEEPSEEK_API_KEY via setx or shell profile, and installing the script on PATH by copy or symlink."},{"claim_ids":["clm_77f453c6f5fa5bce0b17f3791f04517206cbe88926f87ee483b34de3ca5e2540"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states Claude Opus is stronger on complex reasoning, recommending --backend anthropic for hard problems while DeepSeek is comparable on routine tasks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_79365cc07170d0ad05b9891ea3960ae2b545b6d2da3ccd81455e5bd514b5a2a9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Backend switching works mid-session without restart via slash commands, a CLI --switch flag, or VS Code tasks that POST to the proxy's mode endpoint."},{"claim_ids":["clm_87d0e4d80cd9787e07a75fb6e29a853bec628cb3afdb7c8200502c51a3e291d5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A local proxy on localhost:3200 exposes control endpoints: POST /_proxy/mode to switch backends, GET /_proxy/status, and GET /_proxy/cost, forwarding /v1/messages to the active backend."},{"claim_ids":["clm_886d0c6a2de6f7863af35c2fce74e9e8327895e56bc9413e142f40377f86b15c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Remote control mode prints a claude.ai/code session URL usable from a browser, keeping the WebSocket bridge on Anthropic while model calls route through the local proxy."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ad24844036b5d2e52a06e5d6e4292615aae35b03d8d091eca0810e17cdba1980"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI supports flags including --status, --backend (ds/or/fw/anthropic), --cost, --benchmark, --switch, and --remote, per the usage examples."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b8c3083374e2a38acf7ea39d2f836aad77e8e441cb78b9fc1ba52d741eff5f93"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool sets Claude Code environment variables (e.g. ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, model-tier variables) per session and restores original settings on exit rather than persisting them."},{"claim_ids":["clm_df2f2873b71a5ce3656a5c44182210eb57e4b68cb432980097b6ee757d0f748b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented degraded features: no image/vision input through DeepSeek's endpoint, no MCP server tools via the compatibility layer, sequential tool calls by default, and Anthropic cache_control ignored."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e284560b6b4f2f3799eb14e8284c132c293700e3108fc22161292077c6e0308e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product consists of platform launcher scripts (deepclaude.ps1 for Windows, deepclaude.sh for macOS/Linux) plus a Node-based local proxy component."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e6d8ebc3451893026b5439c68d442fd320654961279eca38fefba7340977d4e8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The proxy appears to pass through non-/v1/messages traffic to Anthropic unchanged, so only model API calls are rerouted."}],"claim_ids":["clm_10f056634a8ba8b8c19d9a383d353e5e14f763387c0d820f7213d2807bd6f8fb","clm_55127b79e3a893c302f1682bde7603b03b196c7e3f8c500e5d3d9d7e654ed110","clm_6f7da39702c1469dbdc0ad7fcd32088c414bb9e2c039a57a1c5f896117ebd39f","clm_77f453c6f5fa5bce0b17f3791f04517206cbe88926f87ee483b34de3ca5e2540","clm_79365cc07170d0ad05b9891ea3960ae2b545b6d2da3ccd81455e5bd514b5a2a9","clm_87d0e4d80cd9787e07a75fb6e29a853bec628cb3afdb7c8200502c51a3e291d5","clm_886d0c6a2de6f7863af35c2fce74e9e8327895e56bc9413e142f40377f86b15c","clm_ad24844036b5d2e52a06e5d6e42926